// Coverage: a copattern definition must answer every declared observation.
//
// Coverage (ADR-66 §4.1) is the copattern dual of a `case`'s exhaustiveness --
// the lhs-problem elaboration diagnoses an *unanswered observation*, exactly as
// the Maranget matrix diagnoses a missing constructor. `Point` declares two
// observations, `x` and `depth`; this definition answers only `x`.
//
// Under route (a) the gap surfaces through the codata definition's carrier
// ascription: the record `#{ x = ... }` is checked against `Point`'s carrier
// `#{ x: U_ω (F Integer), depth: U_ω (F Integer) }`, and the ADR-45 record
// former's width+depth discipline rejects the short record with a type mismatch
// that names the unanswered observation `depth`. (A future nominal codata type
// would name the coverage gap more directly; the structural carrier is the
// zero-frozen-core MVP.)
codata Point { x: Integer, depth: Integer }

def rec incomplete() -> Point {
  .x => 0
}

// The golden is the diagnostic naming the unanswered observation `depth`:
//@ expect-diagnostic: depth
